meta {
  name: Sessions - Send Message (Reverb)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/agents/:agent/sessions/:session/turns
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  agent: {{agentId}}
  session: {{agentSessionId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "A customer says their invoice is wrong. What should I do?"
  }
}

docs {
  The same turn `Sessions - Send Message` runs, but the reply is not in the
  response. The request opens the turn (credit check, your message, any
  attachments) and returns `202` with `turn.run_id`; the model call runs on
  the queue and streams to Reverb. Requires the `agent.chat` permission. A
  conversation still answering the previous message, or a workspace out of
  credits, is refused here, before anything is queued.

  Subscribe before sending, to the private channel
  `workspaces.{workspaceId}.agent-sessions.{sessionId}` (authorized by
  `POST /api/broadcasting/auth`). Event names (Echo: prefix with `.`):

  - `turn.changed` — the turn moved. `turn.status` is `running` when
    streaming starts, then `completed`, `awaiting_approval` or `failed`.
    Anything but `running` is the cue to fetch the stored message
    (`turn.message_id`) and, when paused, the waiting actions
    (`turn.pending_action_ids`). `turn.error` is set on `failed`.
  - `turn.delta` — a chunk of assistant text (`run_id`, `text`);
    concatenate in the order received. Chunks are batched, not per token.
  - `turn.tool` — a tool call `started` or `finished` (`tool_call_id`,
    `tool`, `phase`; `arguments` when started and `output` when finished,
    `successful` / `denied` when finished, and `subagent_task_id` for a
    started subagent). `arguments` is left out when larger than 1500 bytes
    and `output` is cut at 1000 characters — the full call is on the stored
    message.
  - `agent.message` — a message was appended (any tab, any teammate).
  - `agent.actions.requested` — the turn paused on actions that need a
    decision; `POST …/sessions/{session}/actions/decisions` records the
    decisions and answers `{ actions, resumed, run_id }` — when `resumed` is
    true the paused turn carries on, streaming the same events for `run_id`.

  Events are not replayed. The transcript is persisted whether or not
  anyone is listening, so a client that connects late or reconnects loads
  `Sessions - List Messages` and uses the socket only for what follows.
}
